   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="edition">
            <ab>
               <lb n="1"/>
               <persName>
                  <name type="gentilicium" key="Aufidia">Aufidia</name>
                  <expan><abbr>C</abbr><ex>ai</ex></expan>
                  <expan><abbr>l</abbr><ex>iberta</ex></expan>
                  <name type="cognomen" key="Optata">Optata</name></persName>,
           <lb n="2"/>
               <persName>
                  <name type="praenomen" key="Caius">
                     <expan><abbr>C</abbr><ex>aius</ex></expan>
                     
                  </name>
                  <name type="gentilicium" key="Aufidius">Aufidius</name>
                  <expan><abbr>C</abbr><ex>ai</ex></expan>
                  <expan><abbr>l</abbr><ex>ibertus</ex></expan>
                  <name type="cognomen" key="Laures">Laures</name></persName>.
        </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="translation">
            <p>Aufidia Optata, freedwoman of Gaius (and) Gaius Aufidius Laure(n)s, freedman of Gaius.</p>
         </div>
         <div type="commentary">
            <p>The text appears to be complete, despite the loss of the left side of the tablet. Optata and Laure(n)s were evidently fellow freedmen (either both were manumitted by the same Gaius Aufidius or one manumitted the other) and were probably life partners.</p>
         </div>
